# Interactive Markers & Queue Optimization

We are addressing two points of friction: the manual entry of timestamps and the perceived "slowness" when managing the job queue.

## Proposed Changes

### [MODIFY] [main_ui.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/main_ui.py)
**Objective 1**: The "Video Marker" Bridge.
- **📍 JS Capture**: We will inject a JavaScript shim into the `video_in` component. 
- **Interactive UI**:
  - **Button: 📍 Capture Start**: Instantly pulls the current playback second from the browser and sets the "Start Point".
  - **Button: 🏁 Capture End**: Grabs the second and automatically calculates the **Duration** relative to your start point.

**Objective 2**: Snappy Queue Control.
- **Immediate Feedback Loop**: Currently, the dashboard waits up to 5 seconds to show changes. I will modify the "Expunge" and "Priority" button listeners to trigger an **immediate status table refresh**. Your jobs will disappear or move the millisecond you click.
- **Logic Cache**: I will stop the "Status Table" from checking the hard drive for preview files on every cycle. We will use a state-flag in memory instead.

### [MODIFY] [pipeline.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/pipeline.py)
**Objective**: Status Flagging.
- The pipeline will set `job.has_preview = True` the moment the muxing finishes. This allows the UI to render the "💾 Preview" icon instantly without slow disk-polling.

## User Action Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> To ensure the **Marker Capture** works perfectly, you must ensure the video is playing or paused at the frame you want. The JS bridge will pull the exact browser-side frame-time.
